### Hardware Configuration and Provisioning

./hardware-configuration.nix is the path that you want the hardware-configuration generated. (Should relay file over ssh and save to location on host.)
```
--generate-hardware-config nixos-generate-config ./hardware-configuration.nix
```

Should be generated into hosts within the proper host dir.

hosts/alpha/hardware-configuration.nix (alpha is a darwin, won't actually have one)


Currently have script anywhere-omen.sh. Planning to integrate it into the flake as a flake app. Can reference flake for needed details (IPs, file paths, etc.). Additionally allows for easy configuration of runners in the future. (Deps guarunteed + nix bonuses).

### Tailscale

Tailscale should check the /var/lib/tailscale folder for existing identities/tailnet membership. If there is one present, the tagged auth key is ignored.

The above is correct, but the nix activation script will not properly evaluate if the file is not present at the path marked in tailscale.nix. Given this, the file should be cleared, but remain in place. (May need to add to persistent files/directories).

TO BE REMOVED - Add comments to tailscale.nix

### Sops Integration

Need to consider potential options here. Current belief is that it should be integrated along with the provisioning script as an extraFiles. Prior to the nixos-anywhere final command, the .sops.yaml file should have the newly provisioned host added and the public key for the machine. (add age to provision script deps, generate keys)

Don't yet have a sops module to import with the declared key dirs and secret files. (Don't yet have any sops secrets).

This has been confirmed as the goal, tied in with provisioning

### Admin/Deploy Keys

The keys are not the same between admin and deploy. Will look into a better naming mechanism to make more clear in the future.

